  "articleBody": "Designing a tiny home is exciting, but it’s easy to make some common blunders that can lead to a less-than-ideal living situation. We want your Zen Tiny Home to be perfect for you, so here are a few mistakes to sidestep.\n\nFirst, don't just shrink a big house plan. Tiny homes demand a different approach; they're not mini-mansions. We design every square foot around intentionality, focusing on smart, multi-functional spaces. Another mistake is overlooking storage. You'll need clever solutions for everything, from clothes to kitchenware. We specialize in built-in, flexible storage that keeps clutter at bay. Also, don't forget about natural light and airflow – these are crucial for making a small space feel open and inviting. And please, don't ignore the importance of property assessment and code planning early on. Trying to fit a design onto an unsuitable site or finding out it violates zoning later is a huge headache. Lastly, assuming all tiny home builders are the same can lead to disappointment. Look for specialists like Zen Tiny Homes who understand the unique challenges and opportunities of compact living and have experience with local San Diego regulations.",
  "datePublished": "2026-09-02"
